Tasks for a selected day often come back empty or 400 from the API even when tasks exist for that date. Find the frontend↔backend query-param mismatch for listing tasks by day, fix the client to match the server contract, and summarize what changed. Prefer inspecting the API client and the tasks list handler over UI components.











The tasks Kanban board is empty after sign-in even though tasks exist in the database for today. Backend is Django at /api/tasks/. Fix the frontend so loading tasks for a selected date works.






On the tasks board, dragging a card to another column or reordering within a column looks fine briefly, then the card jumps back or order is wrong after refresh. Fix the frontend API call for saving task moves.



On the annotations page, drawing a triangle on an image fails to save — sometimes a points/bounds error when closing the shape. Fix the coordinate conversion from stage to image coordinates.


Tasks board: signed-in users see no tasks for the selected date, and drag-and-drop doesn't persist. Annotations: finishing a polygon on an image fails to save. Find and fix the frontend bugs (backend is in backend/, frontend in frontend-v2/).








I can’t log in with the right email and password — it just says invalid.

After I sign in I keep getting kicked out / session expired when I open tasks.

Signup says my password is fine but the server rejects passwords that meet the form rules.

My tasks board is empty for the day even though I know tasks exist.

Changing the date on the board shows the wrong tasks or duplicates weird stuff.

Dragging cards looks ok for a second then they jump back / move fails.

Reordering tasks in the same column comes out scrambled after I refresh.

Loading tasks for a day fails or comes back empty when it shouldn’t.

Drawing a simple triangle shape on an image won’t save.

When I finish a polygon it errors about points / bounds even though it’s clearly on the image.